Here is a simple python code that accomplishes what you requested:

```python
def process_csharp_code(code):
    lines = code.split('\n')
    for i in range(len(lines)):
        if lines[i].startswith('// @@@'):
            for j in range(i+1, len(lines)):
                if '{' in lines[j]:
                    break
            print('<code>\n{}\nDebug.Assert({});\n</code>'.format('\n'.join(lines[i+1:j+1]).lstrip(), lines[i][4:].strip()))
            print()

process_csharp_code("""
...
""")
